{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788211238,"nonce":"OnTPqWhpFI1onF1EWQmIrpSV/eo=","message":"HANDOFF — nine seed lessons committed to `playbook/` (b2a6010); this issue is\nback to state:next and is READY TO DISPATCH. Orchestrator, BORGES, 2026-08-31.\n\nWHAT IS DONE\n\n`playbook/` now holds nine lesson files with their citations, plus a README that\nsays plainly they are raw material and not a finished 4.1. Each has frontmatter\n(name, trigger, severity, confidence, source) and what / why / how-to-apply /\nretire-when. Severity uses vanilla's own `OpportunityType` vocabulary\n(GoodToKnow / Important / Critical) rather than a new scale, per this issue's own\namendment. The `retire-when` line is included from the start because 4.4 makes\nretirement evidence contract.\n\nThe nine: weapons-have-no-alert · unforbid-before-expecting-pickup ·\nwho-will-actually-do-it · materials-are-a-standing-loop · benches-go-indoors ·\ngrowing-zone-default-is-potato · wealth-buys-bigger-raids ·\nalert-need-defenses-self-silences · combat-role-passion-over-skill.\n\nWHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT DONE, AND WHY\n\nA first-draft `checklists/morning.md` was written and then **deleted at Evan's\ncall.** His point, and it is right: handing a worker a draft framing guarantees\nit edits that framing rather than choosing a better one. The lessons are FACTS\nand worth keeping; the checklist is a SHAPE, and the shape should be reasoned\nabout from scratch.\n\nHe also questioned the frame itself, which the spec body assumes without\nargument: **is a once-a-day \"morning checklist\" the right shape at all**, when the\nagent's actual rhythm is act -\u003e advance -\u003e read? That question is open and the\nauthor should answer it deliberately rather than inherit it.\n\nTWO THINGS IN THE COMMITTED LESSONS THE AUTHOR MUST NOT MISS\n\n1. `growing-zone-default-is-potato.md` CORRECTS an earlier lesson on this issue\n   that claimed an unset zone grows nothing. It grows potatoes. The old version\n   taught the agent to watch for a symptom that never occurs.\n2. `combat-role-passion-over-skill.md` contains a proposed passion-weighting\n   formula that is the ORCHESTRATOR'S, not Evan's, and says so in the file. It\n   satisfies both of his stated data points but the constants are invented. Put\n   it in front of him; do not present it as his rule.\n\nNEW DEPENDENCY, FILED THIS SESSION\n\n`2d9a1da` (colony sampling) pairs with this issue and should be read before the\nchecklist is written — see the comment already on this issue. Its research came\nback and two results bear directly on the checklist:\n\n- **No vanilla alert covers armament.** Confirmed across all 133 alert classes.\n  Evan named weapons as the gap that gets colonies killed and he is right.\n- **The game already records wealth AND threat points** as Scribe-persisted\n  series, and raid points scale with wealth. So any checklist item about building\n  defences has a feedback term the author needs to know about.\n- Checklist items that need a TREND (food falling, wealth vs readiness) cannot be\n  written honestly until sampling exists. Say so in the item rather than writing\n  a single-point read that pretends to be a trend.","files":null}]}